      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Find $-4det(A)+3det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2} & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has a zero column, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a triangular matrix, its determinant is given by the product of the elements of the main diagonal: \n\n$$\ndet(B)=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot 3=6\n$$\n\nTherefore, $-4det(A)+3det(B)=-4\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 6=18.$",
